<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Beginners Parking</h1>
<p>Parking is the first skill a new rider actually uses, and for beginners on a 50cc it is also the friendliest one to learn. The machine is light, the footprint is small, and a 50cc slips into curb slots that larger bikes approach with visible reluctance. That said, Hanoi parking has its own etiquette: where to leave the bike, how to leave it, what to take with you, and how the attended lots work. Getting it right from day one saves a beginner the two classic mistakes, a lost number tag and a blocked sidewalk, and it costs nothing but a little attention. The rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, rents 50cc scooters and motorbikes at 200,000 VND per day.</p>
<p>This guide belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental</a> hub, pairs with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost breakdown</a>, and complements the answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The sibling chapters in this beginners series cover choosing a 50cc and riding in city traffic; this page is about the moments between rides.</p>
